<title>JAPAN: Horipro revises down size of planned share buyback.</title>
<headline>Horipro revises down size of planned share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entertainment production company Horipro Inc said on Monday it had revised downward the size of a planned share repurchase, which was announced late last month.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it now plans to buy back 1.2 million of its shares, or up to 1.8 billion yen worth.</p>
<p>On May 28, the company said it would buy back 1.33 million of its shares, or up to two billion yen worth, with the aim of introducing a stock-option scheme.</p>
